onditions, aiming to maintain stable and efficient communication. Both are integral features enhancing the practicality and performance of WIFI communication [Data: Entities (1005), Relationships (1496, 1495)].\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"summary\": \"Security Features: WEP, WPA, WPA2, WPA3, and Client Isolation\",\n      \"explanation\": \"WIFI technology includes optional security protocols designed to protect data transmission. These range from older standards like WEP to more robust ones like WPA, WPA2, and the latest WPA3. Additionally, 'Client Isolation' is an optional feature that enhances security in shared networks by preventing direct communication between devices connected to the same Wi-Fi network. While beneficial for public or shared environments, it can also restrict legitimate inter-device communication [Data: Entities (735, 2753), Relationships (3827)].\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"summary\": \"Wi-Fi 6E introduces the 6 GHz band\",\n      \"explanation\": \"Wi-Fi 6E represents a significant advancement by extending Wi-Fi capabilities into the 6 GHz frequency band. This expansion offers more spectrum, reduced interference, and higher speeds compared to previous generations. The introduction of the 6 GHz band aims to alleviate congestion in the already crowded 2.4 GHz and 5 GHz bands, paving the way for more robust and faster wireless experiences [Data: Entities (757), Relationships (966)].\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"rating\": 7.5,\n  \"rating_explanation\": \"The impact severity rating is high due to the ubiquitous nature of WIFI technology, its critical role in modern communication infrastructure, and the ongoing evolution of its standards and security protocols.\"\n}", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": null, "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": null, "provider_specific_fields": {"refusal": null, "reasoning": null}}, "provider_specific_fields": {"native_finish_reason": "STOP"}}], "created": 1787750861, "model": "google/gemini-2